# Cursor Rules — 冒険者ギルド経営シミュレーション

# 正式な設計文書は AGENTS.md を必ず参照してください。

## Architecture Rules

- This is a Rust desktop app (eframe/egui) for an Adventurer Guild Management Simulation.
- FULLY OFFLINE: No server dependencies, no cloud DB, no network calls. Zero infrastructure cost.
- STRICT SEPARATION: `src/core/` (pure Rust game logic, NO egui dependency) vs `src/ui/` (egui rendering only).
- NEVER import `egui` or `eframe` in any file under `src/core/`.
- Use the "Action pattern" to avoid borrow checker conflicts: collect UI actions as enum variants during `&self` rendering, apply them after drawing with `&mut self`.

## Coding Standards

- Rust 2024 Edition.
- `unsafe` code is DENIED (`unsafe_code = "deny"`).
- All public types must `#[derive(Debug)]`.
- All state structs must `#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]` for JSON save/load.
- Strict Clippy: `clippy::all`, `clippy::pedantic`, `clippy::nursery` enabled. Zero warnings required.
- Deterministic RNG: `rand_pcg::Pcg64` for reproducible randomness.

## Testing

- Unit tests are MANDATORY for all `core` logic.
- Tests must run headlessly: `cargo test` in CI/DevContainer.
- Currently 19 tests passing. Do NOT remove or disable existing tests.

## Domain Model

- Adventurers: 4 statuses (Active/Injured/Retired/Fallen), 7 stats, 11 skill types, age decay at 40+, death at 70-80.
- Quests: Difficulty E-S, 3 client factions (Kingdom/MerchantGuild/Civilian), outcomes: CriticalSuccess/Success/Failure/CriticalFailure.
- Parties: Max 10 members, skill synergy bonuses.
- Monthly Audit: Every 30 days. 3 consecutive failures = game over.
- Guild Rank: F→S. S-rank = game clear.
- Income: Quest commission fees + loot sale margins. Adventurers have no salary.
- Staff: Retired instructors, clerks etc. are salaried (hiring fee + daily/monthly wage).

## File Structure

- `src/main.rs` — Entry point (minimal)
- `src/app.rs` — GuildApp (eframe::App, tab navigation, layout)
- `src/core/` — Game domain (state, adventurer, quest, party, inventory, finance, audit, guild_rank, training, meta)
- `src/ui/` — Rendering (config, font, components/, views/)

## Comments & Documentation

- Preserve all existing comments and docstrings unless directly modifying that code.
- Japanese comments are acceptable and common in this codebase.

## Session Discipline

- Keep changes small and focused. Do not attempt large refactors in a single session.
- Always run `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test` before finishing.
